IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XX -- REMEDIES (ss 238 to 249).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes anyone's point of view.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE READS THE TEXT. As in cb5-part19-investigation.l4: a judgment the Act hands to the
-- court ("the court is satisfied that ...") is a plain BOOLEAN input named for the judgment; a list of
-- orders "the court may make ... including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing" is an
-- enumeration of the listed kinds with one more constructor for every other order, and one rule over the
-- kind; "is not required" and "shall not be stayed" are rules that answer FALSE.
-- Sections 190, 191(4), 214 and 155 are other pieces' ground; each use is a plain input marked
-- "out of range".

§ `Part XX -- Remedies`

§§ `s 238 -- definitions`

-- src:3015 | action means an action under this Act; (action)
@ref CBCA s 238 "action" (src:3015)
GIVEN `it is an action under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `action within s 238` IF
    `it is an action under this Act`

-- The four paragraphs are alternatives (the list is "a, b, c, or d"). (d) is the court's own discretion
-- about a person who fits none of the others; it is a judgment, taken as an input.
-- src:3016 | complainant means
-- src:3017 | (a) a registered holder or beneficial owner, and a former registered holder or beneficial owner, of a security of a corporation or any of its affiliates,
-- src:3018 | (b) a director or an officer or a former director or officer of a corporation or any of its affiliates,
-- src:3019 | (c) the Director, or
-- src:3020 | (d) any other person who, in the discretion of a court, is a proper person to make an application under this Part. (plaignant)
@ref CBCA s 238 "complainant" (src:3016-3020)
GIVEN `the person is a registered holder or beneficial owner, or a former registered holder or beneficial owner, of a security of the corporation or any of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or officer, or a former director or officer, of the corporation or any of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court in its discretion finds the person a proper person to make an application under Part XX` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `complainant within s 238` IF
        `the person is a registered holder or beneficial owner, or a former registered holder or beneficial owner, of a security of the corporation or any of its affiliates`
    OR  `the person is a director or officer, or a former director or officer, of the corporation or any of its affiliates`
    OR  `the person is the Director`
    OR  `the court in its discretion finds the person a proper person to make an application under Part XX`

§§ `s 239 -- derivative action`

-- "Subject to subsection (2)": subsection (1) is who may apply for leave; the conditions precedent of
-- subsection (2) decide whether leave can be given.
-- src:3022 | 239 (1) Subject to subsection (2), a complainant may apply to a court for leave to bring an action in the name and on behalf of a corporation or any of its subsidiaries, or intervene in an action to which any such body corporate is a party, for the purpose of prosecuting, defending or discontinuing the action on behalf of the body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 239(1) (src:3022)
GIVEN `the applicant is a complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is for leave to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the corporation or any of its subsidiaries, or to intervene in an action to which any such body corporate is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to prosecute, defend or discontinue the action on behalf of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a complainant may apply to a court for leave to act for the corporation within s 239(1)` IF
        `the applicant is a complainant`
    AND `the application is for leave to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the corporation or any of its subsidiaries, or to intervene in an action to which any such body corporate is a party`
    AND `the purpose is to prosecute, defend or discontinue the action on behalf of the body corporate`

-- (2)(a): the notice must be given "not less than fourteen days before bringing the application" (so
-- fourteen days is enough), or as the court orders; and the condition applies where the directors "do not
-- bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action". The "if" clause is read as a further
-- requirement of the paragraph (fork F-239-1 in NOTES.md): notice and the directors' inaction are both
-- needed. The court's alternative ("as otherwise ordered by the court") replaces the fourteen days only.
-- src:3025 | (a) the complainant has given notice to the directors of the corporation or its subsidiary of the complainant’s intention to apply to the court under subsection (1) not less than fourteen days before bringing the application, or as otherwise ordered by the court, if the directors of the corporation or its subsidiary do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action;
@ref CBCA s 239(2)(a) (src:3025)
GIVEN `the date the complainant gave the directors notice of the intention to apply` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE
      `the court ordered a different notice period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the condition of notice to the directors is met within s 239(2)(a)` IF
        (    `the date the complainant gave the directors notice of the intention to apply` AT MOST (`the date of the application` MINUS 14)
         OR  `the court ordered a different notice period`)
    AND `the directors do not bring, diligently prosecute or defend or discontinue the action`

-- src:3026 | (b) the complainant is acting in good faith; and
@ref CBCA s 239(2)(b) (src:3026)
GIVEN `the complainant is acting in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the condition of good faith is met within s 239(2)(b)` IF
    `the complainant is acting in good faith`

-- src:3027 | (c) it appears to be in the interests of the corporation or its subsidiary that the action be brought, prosecuted, defended or discontinued.
@ref CBCA s 239(2)(c) (src:3027)
GIVEN `it appears to be in the interests of the corporation or its subsidiary that the action be brought, prosecuted, defended or discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the condition of the interests of the corporation is met within s 239(2)(c)` IF
    `it appears to be in the interests of the corporation or its subsidiary that the action be brought, prosecuted, defended or discontinued`

-- "No action may be brought and no intervention made ... unless the court is satisfied that" (a), (b) and (c):
-- the three are joined by "and", and each is the court's satisfaction.
-- src:3024 | (2) No action may be brought and no intervention in an action may be made under subsection (1) unless the court is satisfied that
@ref CBCA s 239(2) (src:3024)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the condition of notice to the directors is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the complainant is acting in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it appears to be in the interests of the corporation or its subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action may be brought or the intervention made within s 239(2)` IF
        `the court is satisfied that the condition of notice to the directors is met`
    AND `the court is satisfied that the complainant is acting in good faith`
    AND `the court is satisfied that it appears to be in the interests of the corporation or its subsidiary`

§§ `s 240 -- the court's orders in a derivative action`

-- src:3029 | 240 In connection with an action brought or intervened in under section 239, the court may at any time make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:3030 | (a) an order authorizing the complainant or any other person to control the conduct of the action;
-- src:3031 | (b) an order giving directions for the conduct of the action;
-- src:3032 | (c) an order directing that any amount adjudged payable by a defendant in the action shall be paid, in whole or in part, directly to former and present security holders of the corporation or its subsidiary instead of to the corporation or its subsidiary; and
-- src:3033 | (d) an order requiring the corporation or its subsidiary to pay reasonable legal fees incurred by the complainant in connection with the action.
@ref CBCA s 240 (src:3029-3033)
DECLARE `Kind of order in a derivative action (s 240)` IS ONE OF
    `an order authorizing the complainant or any other person to control the conduct of the action (s 240(a))`
    `an order giving directions for the conduct of the action (s 240(b))`
    `an order directing that an amount adjudged payable by a defendant be paid directly to former and present security holders instead of to the corporation or its subsidiary (s 240(c))`
    `an order requiring the corporation or its subsidiary to pay the complainant's reasonable legal fees in connection with the action (s 240(d))`
    `any other order the court thinks fit in connection with the action (s 240)`

-- src:3029 | 240 In connection with an action brought or intervened in under section 239, the court may at any time make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
@ref CBCA s 240 (src:3029)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of order in a derivative action (s 240)`
      `the order is made in connection with an action brought or intervened in under section 239` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order of the kind within s 240` IF
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an order authorizing the complainant or any other person to control the conduct of the action (s 240(a))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an action brought or intervened in under section 239`
    WHEN `an order giving directions for the conduct of the action (s 240(b))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an action brought or intervened in under section 239`
    WHEN `an order directing that an amount adjudged payable by a defendant be paid directly to former and present security holders instead of to the corporation or its subsidiary (s 240(c))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an action brought or intervened in under section 239`
    WHEN `an order requiring the corporation or its subsidiary to pay the complainant's reasonable legal fees in connection with the action (s 240(d))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an action brought or intervened in under section 239`
    WHEN `any other order the court thinks fit in connection with the action (s 240)` THEN `the order is made in connection with an action brought or intervened in under section 239`

§§ `s 241 -- oppression`

-- src:3035 | 241 (1) A complainant may apply to a court for an order under this section.
@ref CBCA s 241(1) (src:3035)
GIVEN `the applicant is a complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a complainant may apply to a court for an order within s 241(1)` IF
    `the applicant is a complainant`

-- (2): the court must be satisfied of one of the three (a)-(c) ("or"), and that the act, the manner of
-- carrying on the business or the exercise of the directors' powers is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial
-- to or unfairly disregards the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer. The
-- characterization is the court's. "Any security holder, creditor, director or officer": the affected
-- person is one of four kinds of party.
-- src:3037 | (2) If, on an application under subsection (1), the court is satisfied that in respect of a corporation or any of its affiliates
-- src:3038 | (a) any act or omission of the corporation or any of its affiliates effects a result,
-- src:3039 | (b) the business or affairs of the corporation or any of its affiliates are or have been carried on or conducted in a manner, or
-- src:3040 | (c) the powers of the directors of the corporation or any of its affiliates are or have been exercised in a manner
-- src:3041 | that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or that unfairly disregards the interests of any security holder, creditor, director or officer, the court may make an order to rectify the matters complained of.
@ref CBCA s 241(2) (src:3037-3041)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 241(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that an act or omission of the corporation or any of its affiliates effects a result` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the business or affairs of the corporation or any of its affiliates are or have been carried on or conducted in a manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the powers of the directors of the corporation or any of its affiliates are or have been exercised in a manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the result or manner is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or unfairly disregards the interests of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person whose interests are affected` IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order to rectify the matters complained of within s 241(2)` IF
        `an application has been made under subsection 241(1)`
    AND (    `the court is satisfied that an act or omission of the corporation or any of its affiliates effects a result`
         OR  `the court is satisfied that the business or affairs of the corporation or any of its affiliates are or have been carried on or conducted in a manner`
         OR  `the court is satisfied that the powers of the directors of the corporation or any of its affiliates are or have been exercised in a manner`)
    AND `the result or manner is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or unfairly disregards the interests of the person`
    AND (    `the person whose interests are affected` EQUALS `a security holder`
         OR  `the person whose interests are affected` EQUALS `a creditor`
         OR  `the person whose interests are affected` EQUALS `a director`
         OR  `the person whose interests are affected` EQUALS `an officer`)

-- src:3043 | (3) In connection with an application under this section, the court may make any interim or final order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:3044 | (a) an order restraining the conduct complained of;
-- src:3045 | (b) an order appointing a receiver or receiver-manager;
-- src:3046 | (c) an order to regulate a corporation’s affairs by amending the articles or by-laws or creating or amending a unanimous shareholder agreement;
-- src:3047 | (d) an order directing an issue or exchange of securities;
-- src:3048 | (e) an order appointing directors in place of or in addition to all or any of the directors then in office;
-- src:3049 | (f) an order directing a corporation, subject to subsection (6), or any other person, to purchase securities of a security holder;
-- src:3050 | (g) an order directing a corporation, subject to subsection (6), or any other person, to pay a security holder any part of the monies that the security holder paid for securities;
-- src:3051 | (h) an order varying or setting aside a transaction or contract to which a corporation is a party and compensating the corporation or any other party to the transaction or contract;
-- src:3052 | (i) an order requiring a corporation, within a time specified by the court, to produce to the court or an interested person financial statements in the form required by section 155 or an accounting in such other form as the court may determine;
-- src:3053 | (j) an order compensating an aggrieved person;
-- src:3054 | (k) an order directing rectification of the registers or other records of a corporation under section 243;
-- src:3055 | (l) an order liquidating and dissolving the corporation;
-- src:3056 | (m) an order directing an investigation under Part XIX to be made; and
-- src:3057 | (n) an order requiring the trial of any issue.
@ref CBCA s 241(3) (src:3043-3057)
DECLARE `Kind of order on an application for relief from oppression (s 241(3))` IS ONE OF
    `an order restraining the conduct complained of (s 241(3)(a))`
    `an order appointing a receiver or receiver-manager (s 241(3)(b))`
    `an order to regulate the corporation's affairs by amending the articles or by-laws or creating or amending a unanimous shareholder agreement (s 241(3)(c))`
    `an order directing an issue or exchange of securities (s 241(3)(d))`
    `an order appointing directors in place of or in addition to the directors in office (s 241(3)(e))`
    `an order directing the corporation or any other person to purchase securities of a security holder (s 241(3)(f))`
    `an order directing the corporation or any other person to pay a security holder part of the money the security holder paid for securities (s 241(3)(g))`
    `an order varying or setting aside a transaction or contract to which the corporation is a party and compensating the corporation or any other party (s 241(3)(h))`
    `an order requiring the corporation to produce financial statements or an accounting to the court or an interested person within a time the court specifies (s 241(3)(i))`
    `an order compensating an aggrieved person (s 241(3)(j))`
    `an order directing rectification of the registers or other records of the corporation under section 243 (s 241(3)(k))`
    `an order liquidating and dissolving the corporation (s 241(3)(l))`
    `an order directing an investigation under Part XIX to be made (s 241(3)(m))`
    `an order requiring the trial of any issue (s 241(3)(n))`
    `any other interim or final order the court thinks fit (s 241(3))`

-- (f) and (g) are "subject to subsection (6)" where the order directs the corporation: an order that the
-- corporation make a payment which subsection (6) forbids is not within the power. An order directing "any
-- other person" is not touched by (6), so the caller says whether the payment is the corporation's.
-- src:3043 | (3) In connection with an application under this section, the court may make any interim or final order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:3049 | (f) an order directing a corporation, subject to subsection (6), or any other person, to purchase securities of a security holder;
-- src:3050 | (g) an order directing a corporation, subject to subsection (6), or any other person, to pay a security holder any part of the monies that the security holder paid for securities;
@ref CBCA s 241(3) (src:3043 src:3049-3050)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of order on an application for relief from oppression (s 241(3))`
      `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order directs the corporation to make a payment that subsection 241(6) forbids` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order of the kind within s 241(3)` IF
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an order restraining the conduct complained of (s 241(3)(a))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order appointing a receiver or receiver-manager (s 241(3)(b))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order to regulate the corporation's affairs by amending the articles or by-laws or creating or amending a unanimous shareholder agreement (s 241(3)(c))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order directing an issue or exchange of securities (s 241(3)(d))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order appointing directors in place of or in addition to the directors in office (s 241(3)(e))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order directing the corporation or any other person to purchase securities of a security holder (s 241(3)(f))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241` AND (NOT `the order directs the corporation to make a payment that subsection 241(6) forbids`)
    WHEN `an order directing the corporation or any other person to pay a security holder part of the money the security holder paid for securities (s 241(3)(g))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241` AND (NOT `the order directs the corporation to make a payment that subsection 241(6) forbids`)
    WHEN `an order varying or setting aside a transaction or contract to which the corporation is a party and compensating the corporation or any other party (s 241(3)(h))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order requiring the corporation to produce financial statements or an accounting to the court or an interested person within a time the court specifies (s 241(3)(i))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order compensating an aggrieved person (s 241(3)(j))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order directing rectification of the registers or other records of the corporation under section 243 (s 241(3)(k))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order liquidating and dissolving the corporation (s 241(3)(l))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order directing an investigation under Part XIX to be made (s 241(3)(m))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `an order requiring the trial of any issue (s 241(3)(n))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`
    WHEN `any other interim or final order the court thinks fit (s 241(3))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 241`

-- (4): the directors' duty and the bar on other amendments. The bar lasts "until a court otherwise orders"
-- and may be lifted case by case "without the consent of the court" is the other way round: consent lifts
-- the bar for that amendment.
-- src:3059 | (4) If an order made under this section directs amendment of the articles or by-laws of a corporation,
-- src:3060 | (a) the directors shall forthwith comply with subsection 191(4); and
@ref CBCA s 241(4) (src:3059-3060)
GIVEN `an order made under section 241 directs amendment of the articles or by-laws of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the directors must forthwith comply with subsection 191(4) within s 241(4)(a)` IF -- out of range: section 191(4) (piece cb4)
    `an order made under section 241 directs amendment of the articles or by-laws of a corporation`

-- src:3059 | (4) If an order made under this section directs amendment of the articles or by-laws of a corporation,
-- src:3061 | (b) no other amendment to the articles or by-laws shall be made without the consent of the court, until a court otherwise orders.
@ref CBCA s 241(4)(b) (src:3059 src:3061)
GIVEN `an order made under section 241 directs amendment of the articles or by-laws of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has consented to the other amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `another amendment to the articles or by-laws is barred within s 241(4)(b)` IF
        `an order made under section 241 directs amendment of the articles or by-laws of a corporation`
    AND (NOT `the court has consented to the other amendment`)
    AND (NOT `a court has otherwise ordered`)

-- (5): the exclusion is from the right to dissent given by s 190, which is another piece's; this rule says
-- only whether subsection (5) removes it.
-- src:3063 | (5) A shareholder is not entitled to dissent under section 190 if an amendment to the articles is effected under this section.
@ref CBCA s 241(5) (src:3063)
GIVEN `an amendment to the articles is effected under section 241` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a shareholder is not entitled to dissent under section 190 within s 241(5)` IF -- out of range: section 190 (piece cb4)
    `an amendment to the articles is effected under section 241`

-- (6): "to a shareholder": the limitation is worded for payments to a shareholder, although paragraphs
-- (3)(f) and (g) speak of a "security holder". A payee who holds only debt obligations is therefore not
-- caught by the words (fork F-241-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3065 | (6) A corporation shall not make a payment to a shareholder under paragraph (3)(f) or (g) if there are reasonable grounds for believing that
-- src:3066 | (a) the corporation is or would after that payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due; or
-- src:3067 | (b) the realizable value of the corporation’s assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities.
@ref CBCA s 241(6) (src:3065-3067)
GIVEN `the payment is to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(f) or (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the realizable value of the corporation's assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation must not make the payment within s 241(6)` IF
        `the payment is to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(f) or (g)`
    AND (    `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due`
         OR  `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the realizable value of the corporation's assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities`)

-- src:3069 | (7) An applicant under this section may apply in the alternative for an order under section 214.
@ref CBCA s 241(7) (src:3069)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant under section 241` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant may apply in the alternative for an order under section 214 within s 241(7)` IF -- out of range: section 214 (piece cb4)
    `the person is an applicant under section 241`

§§ `s 242 -- stay, dismissal, discontinuance and costs`

-- (1): approval by the shareholders is no ground, by itself, for a stay or dismissal; the court may weigh it
-- in an order under s 214, 240 or 241 and in no other.
-- src:3071 | 242 (1) An application made or an action brought or intervened in under this Part shall not be stayed or dismissed by reason only that it is shown that an alleged breach of a right or duty owed to the corporation or its subsidiary has been or may be approved by the shareholders of such body corporate, but evidence of approval by the shareholders may be taken into account by the court in making an order under section 214, 240 or 241.
@ref CBCA s 242(1) (src:3071)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an application or action under Part XX is stayed or dismissed by reason only of approval by the shareholders within s 242(1)` MEANS FALSE

-- src:3071 | 242 (1) An application made or an action brought or intervened in under this Part shall not be stayed or dismissed by reason only that it is shown that an alleged breach of a right or duty owed to the corporation or its subsidiary has been or may be approved by the shareholders of such body corporate, but evidence of approval by the shareholders may be taken into account by the court in making an order under section 214, 240 or 241.
@ref CBCA s 242(1) (src:3071)
GIVEN `the order is made under section 214, 240 or 241` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may take evidence of approval by the shareholders into account within s 242(1)` IF
    `the order is made under section 214, 240 or 241`

-- (2): the steps that need the court's approval. The Quebec step is "failure to respect the agreement
-- between the parties as to the conduct of the proceeding", which replaces want of prosecution there.
-- src:3073 | (2) An application made or an action brought or intervened in under this Part shall not be stayed, discontinued, settled or dismissed for want of prosecution or, in Quebec, failure to respect the agreement between the parties as to the conduct of the proceeding without the approval of the court given on any terms that the court thinks fit and, if the court determines that the interests of any complainant may be substantially affected by such stay, discontinuance, settlement, dismissal or failure, the court may order any party to the application or action to give notice to the complainant.
@ref CBCA s 242(2) (src:3073)
DECLARE `Step in an application or action under Part XX (s 242(2))` IS ONE OF
    `a stay (s 242(2))`
    `a discontinuance (s 242(2))`
    `a settlement (s 242(2))`
    `a dismissal for want of prosecution (s 242(2))`
    `in Quebec, a dismissal for failure to respect the agreement between the parties as to the conduct of the proceeding (s 242(2))`
    `any other step in the application or action (s 242(2))`

-- src:3073 | (2) An application made or an action brought or intervened in under this Part shall not be stayed, discontinued, settled or dismissed for want of prosecution or, in Quebec, failure to respect the agreement between the parties as to the conduct of the proceeding without the approval of the court given on any terms that the court thinks fit and, if the court determines that the interests of any complainant may be substantially affected by such stay, discontinuance, settlement, dismissal or failure, the court may order any party to the application or action to give notice to the complainant.
@ref CBCA s 242(2) (src:3073)
GIVEN step IS A `Step in an application or action under Part XX (s 242(2))`
      `the proceeding is in Quebec` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the approval of the court is required for the step within s 242(2)` IF
    CONSIDER step
    WHEN `a stay (s 242(2))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a discontinuance (s 242(2))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a settlement (s 242(2))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a dismissal for want of prosecution (s 242(2))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in Quebec, a dismissal for failure to respect the agreement between the parties as to the conduct of the proceeding (s 242(2))` THEN `the proceeding is in Quebec`
    WHEN `any other step in the application or action (s 242(2))` THEN FALSE

-- "If the court determines that the interests of any complainant may be substantially affected": the
-- determination is the court's.
-- src:3073 | (2) An application made or an action brought or intervened in under this Part shall not be stayed, discontinued, settled or dismissed for want of prosecution or, in Quebec, failure to respect the agreement between the parties as to the conduct of the proceeding without the approval of the court given on any terms that the court thinks fit and, if the court determines that the interests of any complainant may be substantially affected by such stay, discontinuance, settlement, dismissal or failure, the court may order any party to the application or action to give notice to the complainant.
@ref CBCA s 242(2) (src:3073)
GIVEN `the court determines that the interests of a complainant may be substantially affected by the step` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order a party to give notice to the complainant within s 242(2)` IF
    `the court determines that the interests of a complainant may be substantially affected by the step`

-- src:3075 | (3) A complainant is not required to give security for costs in any application made or action brought or intervened in under this Part.
@ref CBCA s 242(3) (src:3075)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a complainant is required to give security for costs within s 242(3)` MEANS FALSE

-- (4): the court's power is "at any time"; the complainant "may be held accountable" at the end. Both
-- are permissions of the court, open when the application or action is under this Part.
-- src:3077 | (4) In an application made or an action brought or intervened in under this Part, the court may at any time order the corporation or its subsidiary to pay to the complainant interim costs, including legal fees and disbursements, but the complainant may be held accountable for such interim costs on final disposition of the application or action.
@ref CBCA s 242(4) (src:3077)
GIVEN `the application or action is made, brought or intervened in under Part XX` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order the corporation or its subsidiary to pay interim costs to the complainant within s 242(4)` IF
    `the application or action is made, brought or intervened in under Part XX`

-- src:3077 | (4) In an application made or an action brought or intervened in under this Part, the court may at any time order the corporation or its subsidiary to pay to the complainant interim costs, including legal fees and disbursements, but the complainant may be held accountable for such interim costs on final disposition of the application or action.
@ref CBCA s 242(4) (src:3077)
GIVEN `interim costs were ordered under subsection 242(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application or action has reached its final disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the complainant may be held accountable for the interim costs within s 242(4)` IF
        `interim costs were ordered under subsection 242(4)`
    AND `the application or action has reached its final disposition`

§§ `s 243 -- rectification of registers`

-- The three applicants are alternatives. The condition is an allegation (the Act says "alleged to be"), so
-- the court need not have found it.
-- src:3079 | 243 (1) If the name of a person is alleged to be or to have been wrongly entered or retained in, or wrongly deleted or omitted from, the registers or other records of a corporation, the corporation, a security holder of the corporation or any aggrieved person may apply to a court for an order that the registers or records be rectified.
@ref CBCA s 243(1) (src:3079)
GIVEN applicant IS A Party
      `the name of a person is alleged to be or to have been wrongly entered or retained in, or wrongly deleted or omitted from, the registers or other records of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is an aggrieved person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply to a court for an order that the registers or records be rectified within s 243(1)` IF
        `the name of a person is alleged to be or to have been wrongly entered or retained in, or wrongly deleted or omitted from, the registers or other records of a corporation`
    AND (    applicant EQUALS `the corporation`
         OR  applicant EQUALS `a security holder`
         OR  `the applicant is an aggrieved person`)

-- src:3081 | (2) An applicant under this section shall give the Director notice of the application and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 243(2) (src:3081)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 243(2)` IF
    `the person is an applicant under section 243`

-- src:3081 | (2) An applicant under this section shall give the Director notice of the application and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 243(2) (src:3081)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director is entitled to appear and be heard within s 243(2)` IF
    `an application has been made under section 243`

-- src:3083 | (3) In connection with an application under this section, the court may make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:3084 | (a) an order requiring the registers or other records of the corporation to be rectified;
-- src:3085 | (b) an order restraining the corporation from calling or holding a meeting of shareholders or paying a dividend before such rectification;
-- src:3086 | (c) an order determining the right of a party to the proceedings to have their name entered or retained in, or deleted or omitted from, the registers or records of the corporation, whether the issue arises between two or more security holders or alleged security holders, or between the corporation and any security holders or alleged security holders; and
-- src:3087 | (d) an order compensating a party who has incurred a loss.
@ref CBCA s 243(3) (src:3083-3087)
DECLARE `Kind of order on an application to rectify records (s 243(3))` IS ONE OF
    `an order requiring the registers or other records of the corporation to be rectified (s 243(3)(a))`
    `an order restraining the corporation from calling or holding a meeting of shareholders or paying a dividend before rectification (s 243(3)(b))`
    `an order determining the right of a party to have their name entered or retained in, or deleted or omitted from, the registers or records (s 243(3)(c))`
    `an order compensating a party who has incurred a loss (s 243(3)(d))`
    `any other order the court thinks fit on an application to rectify records (s 243(3))`

-- src:3083 | (3) In connection with an application under this section, the court may make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
@ref CBCA s 243(3) (src:3083)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of order on an application to rectify records (s 243(3))`
      `the order is made in connection with an application under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order of the kind within s 243(3)` IF
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an order requiring the registers or other records of the corporation to be rectified (s 243(3)(a))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 243`
    WHEN `an order restraining the corporation from calling or holding a meeting of shareholders or paying a dividend before rectification (s 243(3)(b))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 243`
    WHEN `an order determining the right of a party to have their name entered or retained in, or deleted or omitted from, the registers or records (s 243(3)(c))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 243`
    WHEN `an order compensating a party who has incurred a loss (s 243(3)(d))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 243`
    WHEN `any other order the court thinks fit on an application to rectify records (s 243(3))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an application under section 243`

§§ `s 244 -- directions for the Director`

-- src:3089 | 244 The Director may apply to a court for directions in respect of any matter concerning the Director’s duties under this Act, and on such application the court may give such directions and make such further order as it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 244 (src:3089)
GIVEN `the matter concerns the Director's duties under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may apply to a court for directions within s 244` IF
    `the matter concerns the Director's duties under this Act`

§§ `s 245 -- notice of refusal by the Director`

-- "Within twenty days after receiving them or twenty days after receiving any approval that may be
-- required under any other Act, whichever is later". The later of the two dates; with no approval required,
-- the twenty days run from receipt.
-- src:3091 | 245 (1) If the Director refuses to file any articles or other document that this Act requires the Director to file before the articles or other document become effective, the Director shall, within twenty days after receiving them or twenty days after receiving any approval that may be required under any other Act, whichever is later, give written notice of the refusal to the person who sent the articles or document, giving reasons.
@ref CBCA s 245(1) (src:3091)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the period for the Director to give notice of a refusal within s 245(1)` MEANS
    `Time limit` WITH
        `number of units` IS 20
        `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

-- src:3091 | 245 (1) If the Director refuses to file any articles or other document that this Act requires the Director to file before the articles or other document become effective, the Director shall, within twenty days after receiving them or twenty days after receiving any approval that may be required under any other Act, whichever is later, give written notice of the refusal to the person who sent the articles or document, giving reasons.
@ref CBCA s 245(1) (src:3091)
GIVEN `the date the Director received the articles or other document` IS A DATE
      `the date the Director received any approval required under any other Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal within s 245(1)` IS
    CONSIDER `the date the Director received any approval required under any other Act`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of` `the period for the Director to give notice of a refusal within s 245(1)` `counted from` `the date the Director received the articles or other document`
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        IF `the last day of` `the period for the Director to give notice of a refusal within s 245(1)` `counted from` a GREATER THAN `the last day of` `the period for the Director to give notice of a refusal within s 245(1)` `counted from` `the date the Director received the articles or other document`
        THEN `the last day of` `the period for the Director to give notice of a refusal within s 245(1)` `counted from` a
        ELSE `the last day of` `the period for the Director to give notice of a refusal within s 245(1)` `counted from` `the date the Director received the articles or other document`

-- The duty also asks for reasons; the notice goes to "the person who sent the articles or document".
-- src:3091 | 245 (1) If the Director refuses to file any articles or other document that this Act requires the Director to file before the articles or other document become effective, the Director shall, within twenty days after receiving them or twenty days after receiving any approval that may be required under any other Act, whichever is later, give written notice of the refusal to the person who sent the articles or document, giving reasons.
@ref CBCA s 245(1) (src:3091)
GIVEN `the Director refuses to file the articles or other document that this Act requires the Director to file before they become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the Director gave written notice of the refusal, with reasons, to the person who sent the document` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director has complied with the duty to give notice of the refusal within s 245(1)` IF
        (NOT `the Director refuses to file the articles or other document that this Act requires the Director to file before they become effective`)
    OR  CONSIDER `the date the Director gave written notice of the refusal, with reasons, to the person who sent the document`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST d THEN d AT MOST `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal`

-- (2): deemed refusal, "for the purposes of section 246", if by the last day the Director has neither filed
-- the document nor given written notice of refusal. The question is asked on a date; before the last day
-- has passed there is no deemed refusal yet.
-- src:3093 | (2) If the Director does not file or give written notice of the refusal to file any articles or document within the time limited therefor in subsection (1), the Director is deemed for the purposes of section 246 to have refused to file the articles or document.
@ref CBCA s 245(2) (src:3093)
GIVEN `the date it is asked whether the Director is deemed to have refused` IS A DATE
      `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal` IS A DATE
      `the date the Director filed the articles or document` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the Director gave written notice of the refusal to file` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director is deemed to have refused to file the document for the purposes of s 246 within s 245(2)` IF
        `the date it is asked whether the Director is deemed to have refused` GREATER THAN `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal`
    AND (CONSIDER `the date the Director filed the articles or document`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST f THEN f GREATER THAN `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the date the Director gave written notice of the refusal to file`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST g THEN g GREATER THAN `the last day for the Director to give written notice of the refusal`)

§§ `s 246 -- appeal from the Director's decision`

-- src:3095 | 246 A person who feels aggrieved by a decision of the Director referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (g) may apply to a court for an order, including an order requiring the Director to change the decision
-- src:3096 | (a) to refuse to file in the form submitted any articles or other document required by this Act to be filed;
-- src:3097 | (b) to give a name, to change or revoke a name, or to refuse to reserve, accept, change or revoke a name under section 12;
-- src:3098 | (c) to grant, or to refuse to grant, an exemption that may be granted under this Act and the regulations;
-- src:3099 | (d) to refuse under subsection 187(11) to permit a continued reference to shares having a nominal or par value;
-- src:3100 | (e) to refuse to issue a certificate of discontinuance under section 188 or a certificate attesting that as of a certain date the corporation exists under subsection 263.1(2);
-- src:3101 | (f) to issue, or to refuse to issue, a certificate of revival under section 209, or the decision with respect to the terms for revival imposed by the Director;
-- src:3102 | (f.1) to correct, or to refuse to correct, articles, a notice, a certificate or other document under section 265;
-- src:3103 | (f.2) to cancel, or to refuse to cancel, the articles and related certificate under section 265.1; or
-- src:3104 | (g) to dissolve a corporation under section 212.
-- src:3105 | The Court may make any order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 246 (src:3095-3105)
DECLARE `Kind of decision of the Director that may be appealed (s 246)` IS ONE OF
    `a decision to refuse to file in the form submitted articles or another document required to be filed (s 246(a))`
    `a decision to give a name, to change or revoke a name, or to refuse to reserve, accept, change or revoke a name under section 12 (s 246(b))`
    `a decision to grant, or to refuse to grant, an exemption that may be granted under this Act and the regulations (s 246(c))`
    `a decision to refuse under subsection 187(11) to permit a continued reference to shares having a nominal or par value (s 246(d))`
    `a decision to refuse to issue a certificate of discontinuance under section 188 or a certificate attesting that the corporation exists under subsection 263.1(2) (s 246(e))`
    `a decision to issue, or to refuse to issue, a certificate of revival under section 209, or the terms for revival imposed by the Director (s 246(f))`
    `a decision to correct, or to refuse to correct, articles, a notice, a certificate or other document under section 265 (s 246(f.1))`
    `a decision to cancel, or to refuse to cancel, the articles and related certificate under section 265.1 (s 246(f.2))`
    `a decision to dissolve a corporation under section 212 (s 246(g))`
    `any other decision of the Director (s 246)`

-- "A person who feels aggrieved": the feeling is the person's, so it is an input and not tested.
-- src:3095 | 246 A person who feels aggrieved by a decision of the Director referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (g) may apply to a court for an order, including an order requiring the Director to change the decision
@ref CBCA s 246 (src:3095)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of decision of the Director that may be appealed (s 246)`
      `the person feels aggrieved by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person may apply to a court for an order on the decision within s 246` IF
        `the person feels aggrieved by the decision`
    AND CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `a decision to refuse to file in the form submitted articles or another document required to be filed (s 246(a))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a decision to give a name, to change or revoke a name, or to refuse to reserve, accept, change or revoke a name under section 12 (s 246(b))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a decision to grant, or to refuse to grant, an exemption that may be granted under this Act and the regulations (s 246(c))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a decision to refuse under subsection 187(11) to permit a continued reference to shares having a nominal or par value (s 246(d))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a decision to refuse to issue a certificate of discontinuance under section 188 or a certificate attesting that the corporation exists under subsection 263.1(2) (s 246(e))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a decision to issue, or to refuse to issue, a certificate of revival under section 209, or the terms for revival imposed by the Director (s 246(f))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a decision to correct, or to refuse to correct, articles, a notice, a certificate or other document under section 265 (s 246(f.1))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a decision to cancel, or to refuse to cancel, the articles and related certificate under section 265.1 (s 246(f.2))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a decision to dissolve a corporation under section 212 (s 246(g))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `any other decision of the Director (s 246)` THEN FALSE

-- "The Court may make any order it thinks fit": open once an application under s 246 is before it.
-- src:3105 | The Court may make any order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 246 (src:3105)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 246` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make any order it thinks fit on the appeal within s 246` IF
    `an application has been made under section 246`

§§ `s 247 -- restraining or compliance order`

-- Applicant: a complainant or a creditor of the corporation (alternatives). Respondent: the corporation or
-- one of nine kinds of person connected with it. The ground: the respondent does not comply with the Act,
-- the regulations, the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement. "In addition to any
-- other right they have": the section is not exclusive.
-- src:3107 | 247 If a corporation or any director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary, auditor, trustee, receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator or liquidator of a corporation does not comply with this Act, the regulations, articles or by-laws, or a unanimous shareholder agreement, a complainant or a creditor of the corporation may, in addition to any other right they have, apply to a court for an order directing any such person to comply with, or restraining any such person from acting in breach of, any provisions of this Act, the regulations, articles or by-laws, or a unanimous shareholder agreement, and on such application the court may so order and make any further order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 247 (src:3107)
GIVEN `the applicant is a complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a creditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent is the corporation or a director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary, auditor, trustee, receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator or liquidator of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent does not comply with this Act, the regulations, the articles or by-laws, or a unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply to a court for a compliance or restraining order within s 247` IF
        (    `the applicant is a complainant`
         OR  `the applicant is a creditor of the corporation`)
    AND `the respondent is the corporation or a director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary, auditor, trustee, receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator or liquidator of the corporation`
    AND `the respondent does not comply with this Act, the regulations, the articles or by-laws, or a unanimous shareholder agreement`

§§ `s 248 -- summary application`

-- src:3109 | 248 Where this Act states that a person may apply to a court, the application may be made in a summary manner by petition, originating notice of motion, or otherwise as the rules of the court provide, and subject to any order respecting notice to interested parties or costs, or any other order the court thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 248 (src:3109)
GIVEN `this Act states that a person may apply to a court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application may be made in a summary manner within s 248` IF
    `this Act states that a person may apply to a court`

§§ `s 249 -- appeal of an order`

-- src:3111 | 249 (1) An appeal lies to the court of appeal of a province from any final order made by a court of that province under this Act.
-- src:3112 | Appeal with leave
-- src:3113 | (2) An appeal lies to the court of appeal of a province from any order other than a final order made by a court of that province, only with leave of the court of appeal in accordance with the rules applicable to that court.
@ref CBCA s 249 (src:3111-3113)
DECLARE `Whether an appeal lies (s 249)` IS ONE OF
    `an appeal lies to the court of appeal of the province as of right (s 249(1))`
    `an appeal lies to the court of appeal of the province only with its leave (s 249(2))`
    `s 249 gives no appeal`

-- A final order: as of right. Any other order: only with leave. An order not made by a court of a province
-- under this Act is outside the section.
-- src:3111 | 249 (1) An appeal lies to the court of appeal of a province from any final order made by a court of that province under this Act.
-- src:3112 | Appeal with leave
-- src:3113 | (2) An appeal lies to the court of appeal of a province from any order other than a final order made by a court of that province, only with leave of the court of appeal in accordance with the rules applicable to that court.
@ref CBCA s 249 (src:3111-3113)
GIVEN `the order was made by a court of a province under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is a final order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether an appeal lies (s 249)`
DECIDE `whether an appeal lies within s 249` IS
    IF NOT `the order was made by a court of a province under this Act`
    THEN `s 249 gives no appeal`
    ELSE IF `the order is a final order`
         THEN `an appeal lies to the court of appeal of the province as of right (s 249(1))`
         ELSE `an appeal lies to the court of appeal of the province only with its leave (s 249(2))`
